. Relevant to cause-and-effect analysis.", "newValue": "The Internet Society, established on December 11, 1992, in Reston, Virginia, is a prominent organization dedicated to promoting the open development, evolution, and use of the Internet for the benefit of all people globally. Founded by notable figures including Vint Cerf and Bob Kahn, the organization plays a critical role in shaping Internet policy and ensuring its accessibility and security across various regions. Its significance in contemporary history lies in its advocacy for the principles of an open Internet, which has profound implications for communications, commerce, education, and human rights.

